        "direction": "horizontal",
        "gap": "sm",
        "align": "center"
      },
      "children": [
        "causes_icon",
        "causes_title"
      ]
    },
    "causes_icon": {
      "type": "Icon",
      "props": {
        "name": "../assets/r_000294_01_2_exclamation-triangle.svg"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "causes_title": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Primary Causes and Contributing Factors",
        "variant": "h2"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "causes_intro_text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "The crisis originated from several interconnected issues within the financial system:"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "subprime_mortgages_stack": {
      "type": "Stack",
      "props": {
        "direction": "vertical",
        "gap": "sm"
      },
      "children": [
        "subprime_mortgages_label",
        "subprime_mortgages_text"
      ]
    },
    "subprime_mortgages_label": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Subprime Mortgages",
        "variant": "label"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "subprime_mortgages_text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Lenders provided mortgages to borrowers with poor credit histories and high debt-to-income ratios, often with little to no documentation. These \"subprime\" loans typically featured adjustable-rate terms that started with low payments but reset to much higher rates after a few years, making them unaffordable for many borrowers."
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "financial_deregulation_stack": {
      "type": "Stack",
      "props": {
        "direction": "vertical",
        "gap": "sm"
      },
      "children": [
        "financial_deregulation_label",
        "financial_deregulation_text"
      ]
    },
    "financial_deregulation_label": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Financial Deregulation",
        "variant": "label"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "financial_deregulation_text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "A period of relaxed financial regulation, including the repeal of the Glass-Steagall Act in 1999 (which separated commercial and investment banking), allowed financial institutions to take on greater risks. This lack of oversight extended to complex financial instruments and the shadow banking system."
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "housing_bubble_stack": {
      "type": "Stack",
      "props": {
        "direction": "vertical",
        "gap": "sm"
      },
      "children": [
        "housing_bubble_label",
        "housing_bubble_text"
      ]
    },
    "housing_bubble_label": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Housing Bubble",
        "variant": "label"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "housing_bubble_text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Low interest rates, coupled with the proliferation of subprime mortgages, fueled a speculative housing bubble. As home prices soared, many homeowners extracted equity, and lenders assumed increasing risk, believing house prices would continue to rise indefinitely."
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "securitization_stack": {
      "type": "Stack",
      "props": {
        "direction": "vertical",
        "gap": "sm"
      },
      "children": [
        "securitization_label",
        "securitization_text"
      ]
    },
    "securitization_label": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Securitization and Derivatives",
        "variant": "label"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "securitization_text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Subprime mortgages were packaged into complex financial products like Mortgage-Backed Securities (MBS) and Collateralized Debt Obligations (CDOs). These instruments were then sold to investors worldwide, often receiving inflated ratings from credit agencies, masking their inherent risk. Credit Default Swaps (CDS), an insurance-like derivative, further amplified the risk by allowing speculation on the default of these securities."
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "predatory_lending_stack": {
      "type": "Stack",
      "props": {
        "direction": "vertical",
        "gap": "sm"
      },
      "children": [
        "predatory_lending_label",
        "predatory_lending_text"
      ]
    },
    "predatory_lending_label": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Predatory Lending",
        "variant": "label"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "predatory_lending_text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Aggressive lending practices, often targeting vulnerable borrowers, included offering loans with hidden fees, complex terms, and penalties for early repayment, which contributed to the unsustainability of the mortgage market."
      },
      "children": []
    },
